  "funFact": "Tortoises and tuataras both look like primordial reptiles frozen in time — but they are on opposite sides of the reptile family tree. The tree splits into two main branches: one leading to lizards, snakes, and tuataras, the other to turtles, dinosaurs, birds, and crocs. Despite both looking equally ancient, a tortoise is on the dinosaur side and a tuatara is on the lizard side.",
